  "eml_eudora.eml": {
    "content_type": "message/rfc822",
    "params": {
      "charset": "utf-8"
    },
    "metadata": {
      "dc:description": "this sounds like an excellent idea... what is the best way to proceed to make this happen? c",
      "dc:title": "eml eudora",
      "dc:type": "Text",
      "metadata:kind": "email"
    },
    "markdown": "this sounds like an excellent idea...\\\nwhat is the best way to proceed to make this happen?\n\nc\n\n-----Original Message-----\\\nFrom: Alex Morgan \\[mailto:alex@example.com\\]\\\nSent: 24 August 2001 10:25\\\nTo: sam@example.com; chris@example.com\\\nSubject: RE: ieee and acm membership\n\nit works on individual basis. much like an MSDN account.\n\n> -----Original Message-----\\\n> From: Sam Taylor \\[mailto:sam@example.com\\]\\\n> Sent: Friday, August 24, 2001 10:16 AM\\\n> To: 'Alex Morgan'; chris@example.com\\\n> Subject: RE: ieee and acm membership\n\n> top idea. but isn't it possible to get a \"example\" account\\\n> and give each employee access to this account?\n\n> sam\n\n> > -----Original Message-----\\\n> > From: Alex Morgan \\[mailto:alex@example.com\\]\\\n> > Sent: Thursday, August 23, 2001 11:55\\\n> > To: sam@example.com; chris@example.com\\\n> > Subject: ieee and acm membership\n\n> > Hi,\n\n> > Do you think it'd be a good idea if Example pays for an\\\n> > IEEE Computer\\\n> > Society and/or ACM memberships for Example employees that\n\n> wish this?\n\n> > We could package a free IEEE and/or ACM membership as a\\\n> > Example employee\\\n> > benefit.\n\n> > ACM: http://www.acm.org\\\n> > IEEE: http://www.ieee.org\n\n> > Robin and myself are already members of IEEE, I'm also a\\\n> > member of ACM.\n\n> > Cost is about $150 per year for each per person.\n\n> > Greets,\\\n> > Alex\n"
  },
  "mbox_eudora.mbx": {
    "content_type": "application/mbox",
    "params": {
      "charset": "utf-8"
    },
    "metadata": {
      "dc:title": "mbox eudora",
      "dc:type": "Collection",
      "mbox:date-end": "2002-02-15T14:29:36Z",
      "mbox:messages": "4",
      "mbox:senders": "Ada Lovelace; charles@example.com; José",
      "mbox:date-start": "2002-02-11T13:10:00Z",
      "mbox:subjects": "Engine notes; Lunch?; Café mécanique",
      "metadata:kind": "mailbox"
    },
    "markdown": "# Engine notes\n\n- **From:** Ada Lovelace \\<ada@example.com\\>\n- **To:** Charles Babbage \\<charles@example.com\\>\n- **Date:** Mon, 11 Feb 2002 13:10 +0000\n\nCharles,\n\nFrom the start, the engine was meant to weave patterns.\\\nFrom what I hear, the cards are ready.\n\nAda\n\n# Lunch?\n\n- **From:** charles@example.com\n- **To:** ada@example.com\n- **Date:** Tue, 12 Feb 2002 10:02 +0000\n\nLunch on Thursday?\n\n# (no subject)\n\n- **From:** Ada Lovelace \\<ada@example.com\\>\n- **To:** charles@example.com\n- **Date:** Wed, 13 Feb 2002 09:29 +0000\n- **Attachments:** plan.doc\n\nThe plan is attached.\n\n# Café mécanique\n\n- **From:** José \\<jose@example.org\\>\n- **To:** ada@example.com\n- **Date:** Fri, 15 Feb 2002 15:29 +0100\n\nThe mechanical café opens on Monday.\n"
  },
